1
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:31,960
Holy crap!

2
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,500
Are you kidding me?

3
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,200
Oniwa Banshu are down!

4
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:38,520
The Mimawari Kuma are toast!

5
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,360
We got no one left!

6
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:42,050
Daikoku!

7
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:43,760
Kazukage!

8
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,620
Captain Head!

9
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,060
I knew he had a reputation,
but I wasn't expecting this.

10
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:54,302
He didn't just resist the virus.

11
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:56,655
He used its power to wreck our troops.

12
00:01:56,920 --> 00:02:00,877
I see why the land of Juana has
remained untouched for so many years.

13
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,600
It's an island of monsters.

14
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:12,360
Vos, no!

15
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,640
Is this the only way?

16
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:22,920
What are you waiting for, Yadda-Bee?

17
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:28,360
Empty your mind and calm yourself.

18
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:31,480
You know what'll happen
if I become an Oni.

19
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:37,820
I'm sorry.

20
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:40,551
Please give me a second to compose myself.

21
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:42,080
I'll do it soon.

22
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,960
I'll do it now!

23
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,820
I do not envy you.

24
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,780
Of course it's hard.

25
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:53,180
He is like a father to us.

26
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:00,920
I'm losing control, Sangoro! Do it!

27
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,020
You won't go alone, boss!

28
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,260
I shall be with you soon!

29
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,320
Come on, please!

30
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:15,997
Can't you help them, Mr.

31
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:16,910
Raccoon?

32
00:03:16,993 --> 00:03:18,000
There's no time!

33
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,026
There's no saving me anymore!

34
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:21,827
You don't have to be afraid!

35
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,420
Now cut me down!

36
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,191
I don't want to hurt you!

37
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:35,597
If you don't do it, I won't
be able to control myself.

38
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:38,617
We have done our best, but this is it.

39
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:42,077
Mr Raccoon, if we don't get that cure now,

40
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:47,420
this whole floor, all of our friends
will become ice! It's Oni again.

41
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,440
Help us, Master Queen!

42
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,040
Master Queen!

43
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:59,077
All of your men have
served you faithfully.

44
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:02,572
Why do we have to die from
your virus alongside the enemy?

45
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,110
Buzz off!

46
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,940
Why should I lift a finger for you?

47
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:13,700
You peons aren't worth saving!

48
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,940
You ever consider that?

49
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:18,320
Listen, morons.

50
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:22,246
If I don't have any use for you,
you're no better than garbage.

51
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:29,800
Show some respect.

52
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:32,240
That virus is my masterpiece.

53
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:36,180
In fact, it was created to
erase your deficiencies.

54
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,240
You hear that, Pleasures?

55
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,757
You already lost the Devil Fruit Lottery,

56
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,977
so it's not like you're gonna
ever amount to anything.

57
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:46,600
You're nothing but giggling cannon fodder.

58
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,300
Ha ha, ha, ha, cruel!

59
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:55,700
As for you waiters, no matter how long
you wait, no more smile fruits are coming.

60
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,620
You lost your chance.

61
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,076
You'd know better than the pleasures.

62
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:02,560
The eternal waiters.

63
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:06,120
A living tragedy, a colossal
monument to failure.

64
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,617
The only way you scrubs can help the beast

65
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:12,037
pirates is to become an
oni and cause some chaos!

66
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,500
before you kick the bucket! Ya dig?

67
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:18,120
It's better to burn out than fade away.

68
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:21,800
Wait, this is like
you're telling us to die?

69
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,640
And why not?

70
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,920
We have more than enough troops.

71
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:31,980
How could you say that?

72
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,360
You're sick!

73
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:35,560
I gave you a chance!

74
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,901
That antibody could save
a couple of you at least!

75
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:45,490
Damn it.

76
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:47,640
I'm not going to die like this.

77
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:49,015
Cut down the samurai.

78
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,160
Cut down the oni.

79
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:51,714
Every man for himself.

80
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:55,860
Now you're motivated.

81
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:58,104
Some of you might even survive.

82
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,580
This guy is a monster.

83
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,517
I can't believe they follow him.

84
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,306
Well, that's pirates for you.

85
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:06,980
Listen up, you damned samurai.

86
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:10,697
You might want to think about
what you're protecting right now.

87
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:17,120
Now, that raccoon made some big
promises, but he's a pirate just like us.

88
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,280
Don't you dare.

89
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:23,520
You really think he can mass-produce
antibodies that quickly?

90
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,740
He tricked you!

91
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:28,837
He was infected as well.

92
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:32,626
He probably took the antibody
for himself and got the hell out.

93
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,100
The Straw Hats are nothing like you!

94
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:39,477
How can you be so sure?

95
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:41,760
You think pirates have morals?

96
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:50,960
This may be farewell for now, but
I'll follow you sooner or later boss.

97
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:56,220
Don't be so hasty to follow!

98
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:10,910
Farewell.

99
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,180
Don't do it!

100
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,300
What the hell?

101
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:33,700
Please, Mr.

102
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:35,637
Raccoon, don't try and stop me.

103
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,760
We're losing him.

104
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:37,917
This was his choice.

105
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,620
I'm going to save him!

106
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:41,080
Stand back and watch!

107
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:43,720
This will work!

108
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:44,980
Swallow it, boss!

109
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,000
That was close!

110
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,460
You guys scared me!

111
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:55,880
So, did that fix him?

112
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,100
All right!

113
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,860
It's working fine! See?

114
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:04,420
His body's warming up!

115
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,826
Oh, you're not dead, are you?

116
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,588
Tell me you're alive, boss.

117
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,360
I am.

118
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,980
Yes, I knew you could
do it, Mr. Raccoon Dog.

119
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,520
The boss is okay.

120
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,140
Yuck! Tristan!

121
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:39,518
You'd better hurry!

122
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,980
We're on it, Dr. Chopper!

123
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,140
Is that a cannon?

124
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,500
Okay, it's ready.

125
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:52,898
Just give the word.

126
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,080
Oh, let me get attacked!

127
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,030
Dr.

128
00:09:00,113 --> 00:09:01,920
Chopper, do the honors!

129
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:03,160
Wait, what?

130
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:08,140
My Shuffer-Fade Snap-Do-Lyzer!

131
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:11,850
Fire! Fire!

132
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,500
Happy one!

133
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,580
Inhale the mist!

134
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,540
What the hell do you think
you're doing, you damn raccoon?

135
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:45,640
You've destroyed my masterpiece!

136
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:48,240
How did you even pull that off?

137
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:52,500
Even with the cure,

138
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,757
it's impossible to give
the medicine to everyone on

139
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,537
the floor since you made sure
to infect so many people.

140
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:02,040
So I crafted a virus out of the
antibody, one that spreads just as fast.

141
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:03,580
You what?

142
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:07,417
If you can make a bad virus, I
can beat it with a good virus.

143
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:10,157
I had to get creative and
distribute it through mist.

144
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:12,820
But all they need to do is breathe it in!

145
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:18,760
You're just a doctor from
a ratty little pirate crew!

146
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:21,477
How the hell did you
learn a trick like that?

147
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:24,917
Because our crew has traveled the
world and trained with the best!

148
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,588
Also, you got some nerve
healing, my flunky!

149
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,537
Stay in your lane, dammit!

150
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:31,440
Their lives are mine!

151
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:36,757
I'm cleaning up your mess after you
let a deadly virus get out of hand!

152
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:39,546
That isn't a weapon you
should use so lightly!

153
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:46,960
I am a genius, dammit!

154
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:50,860
You think I need a raccoon
to teach me ethics? Learn!

155
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:01,990
Pleasures!

156
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:05,380
You saved me!

157
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:12,597
Get out of my way, if you want to die
so bad, then do it somewhere else!

158
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,020
Shut up, queen!

159
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:19,137
Our brothers were almost killed
by you, and for what? Mr.

160
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,280
Raccoon here saved our lives!

161
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:26,697
So tell me, what do we have to gain
for working for a maniac like you?

162
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:31,197
At least we can die for someone worth
protecting, ain't that right, guys?

163
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,680
Let's hear it!

164
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:39,040
Thanks, Mr. Raccoon! Mr. Raccoon!

165
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,540
Sir Raccoon!

166
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,780
No, Dr. Raccoon!

167
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:46,300
I'm forever in your debt, Mr. Raccoon! Mr.

168
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,000
Raccoon, that was amazing!

169
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,837
The Straw Hacks are lucky.

170
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,400
That's one good raccoon.

171
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,060
Go, Raccoon!

172
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:54,220
You're the best!

173
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:55,397
Go, Raccoon!

174
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,700
You're the best!

175
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,937
Go, Raccoon!

176
00:11:58,020 --> 00:11:59,140
You're the best!

177
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:00,377
Go, Raccoon!

178
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:01,537
You're the best!

179
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,380
You can go to hell, queen!

180
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:10,360
You think I need you, chumps?

181
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,740
What the hell is this?

182
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,340
Nice work back there, raccoon.

183
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,120
Now do it.

184
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,020
You got it, Marco.

185
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:25,752
But there's one last thing I want to say.

186
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:28,760
I'll kill you, raccoon.

187
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:30,510
Rumble.

188
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:33,260
Monster point!

189
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:35,810
No!

190
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,900
I'm not a raccoon!

191
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:45,430
Fine!

192
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:47,830
Oops!

193
00:12:47,913 --> 00:12:48,940
I'm sorry!

194
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:56,717
If we climb through the ceiling, we can
hide in the space between the floors.

195
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,517
I doubt anyone will look for us in there.

196
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,430
That's good.

197
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:00,880
Lord Momonosuke.

198
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:03,337
It's going on a little while longer.

199
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,860
Be brave, Momonosuke.

200
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:06,500
I know you can do this.

201
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:09,560
In truth, my heart is in turmoil.

202
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,940
Yamato and I have dispatched
every foe in sight.

203
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:20,474
Not because of our foes, but
because of my helplessness.

204
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:22,260
I'm a useless burden.

205
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:25,430
Enough!

206
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,379
You all think far too highly of me!

207
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:30,700
I have nothing! Nothing!

208
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:36,040
I am but a fool.

209
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,140
I am spineless and weak.

210
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:40,720
I am not worth defending.

211
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:42,540
Just let me die.

212
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:45,233
I think you're perfectly great, my lord.

213
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,520
There's nothing great about me.

214
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,898
You must give yourself time to grow.

215
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:56,400
Yes, you may be small right now, but someday
I know you'll grow into a fine shogun.

216
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,797
You'll be a great man someday.

217
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,821
You can surpass even Kozuki Oden.

218
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,740
You're just saying that.

219
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,280
It's not true.

220
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:07,320
It's not true at all!

221
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,340
I am a failure!

222
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:14,510
Huh?

223
00:14:14,593 --> 00:14:15,423
You're an eel?

224
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:17,420
Lord Momonosuke!

225
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:20,357
I'm afraid I don't understand.

226
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:23,060
And this happens when he's troubled.

227
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:27,541
He's unable to return to his human
form until his heart is at ease.

228
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:29,600
But you weren't born this way.

229
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:31,742
Momo, did you eat a Devil Fruit?

230
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,120
I did.

231
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:46,560
Speaking of Kaido,

232
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:51,014
Remember when the Navy captured
him all those years ago?

233
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,110
Dr.

234
00:14:54,193 --> 00:14:57,940
Vegapunk took the opportunity to
extract his bloodline elements,

235
00:14:58,180 --> 00:15:01,120
then made an artificial
Devil Fruit from it.

236
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:04,917
Naturally, the world government
asked him to hand it over,

237
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:09,140
but in the end, his creation was
viewed as a disappointing failure.

238
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:13,675
However, they kept the fruit on Punk
Hazard instead of throwing it away.

239
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:17,080
Why are you bringing that up now?

240
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:19,097
Punk Hazard was wiped out.

241
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,397
It's nothing more than a memory.

242
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:24,360
I hope it was destroyed in the explosion.

243
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,517
But a team from Naval
Base G5 reported that one

244
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,306
facility on the island
was still in operation.

245
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:39,142
Well, if it was a failure, at least we know
there won't be another Kaido out there!

246
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,417
Who was it that patched us up?

247
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,497
That's still a mystery.

248
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,917
I thought I saw our benefactor.

249
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,457
But no, I must have been dreaming.

250
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:04,280
I dare say it's impossible!

251
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:11,537
While we sit here, sir, Luffy and his
friends are fighting Kaido on our behalf.

252
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:15,700
Even if we are injured, we must
return to the battle at hand.

253
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:18,760
We cannot relent until victory is ours!

254
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,240
Let us go!

255
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,940
While we still have our lives to give.

256
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,620
My loyal retainers!

257
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,477
You've had a rough run of it, haven't you?

258
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:32,600
How I've missed you all!

259
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:40,980
I see the years haven't been kind to you!

260
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:45,790
Huh?

261
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:50,410
It's...

262
00:16:50,493 --> 00:16:52,280
it's Lord Odin!

263
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:56,620
It is you...

264
00:16:57,480 --> 00:17:03,300
I can't blame you for being surprised.

265
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:06,564
I was sent to the future
thanks to Toki's power.

266
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,380
I shall explain it later.

267
00:17:08,780 --> 00:17:09,740
What a tale!

268
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,857
My lord Odin!

269
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,175
It's truly a miracle!

270
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:17,940
Sorry to make you wait,

271
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:22,380
but we'll have time to celebrate
our reunion once the battle is won!

272
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:25,760
Now follow me!

273
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:29,180
We failed to slay Kaido
once, but not this time!

274
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:30,850
Of course.

275
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:32,520
We shall come with you.

276
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:34,800
I could ask for nothing more.

277
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,440
Let us go forth.

278
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:43,200
My Samurai, you're as loyal
as you were the day we parted!

279
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:47,220
Dammit, everyone stop!

280
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:49,760
This can't be Lord Oden.

281
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:50,900
Who are you?

282
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,000
Answer me!

283
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,880
Ashina, my friend! Kinema!

284
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,520
What did Lady Toki say?

285
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,880
We may lack the power needed
to return to the past.

286
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:04,420
However, we're able to leap ahead.

287
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:11,840
The past cannot be
altered, no matter what.

288
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:15,540
Lady Toki was only able to
send people to the future,

289
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:18,177
but she couldn't have
done that to Lord Odin.

290
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,460
They both died.

291
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:23,580
The history of that dark
day cannot be rewritten.

292
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:27,880
All we can do is bury our
regret and fight for tomorrow.

293
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,597
Just so, and we'll do it beside our Lord.

294
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:34,780
We can't.

295
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:40,200
I've had enough!

296
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:47,220
How did your senses kill him on?

297
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:49,020
Check this!

298
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:53,010
Look!

299
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:54,733
He's not even bleeding!

300
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:57,580
What? How?

301
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,057
Oh, Ashura.

302
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:05,220
What shameful behavior from a man who
pledged his undying loyalty to me!

303
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,580
What say you?

304
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:10,200
Will you be my samurai?

305
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:15,360
Watch out!

306
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:18,450
Ashura!

307
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:28,440
You've shown your true
colors, haven't you?

308
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:33,060
We all felt the same.

309
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:39,740
I wish that Lord Odin had returned to
us, but this is a snake in his guise.

310
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,340
What a cruel trick.

311
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:44,717
But if that's not Lord Odin,
then who are we dealing with?

312
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:46,800
He'll pay for getting my hopes up.

313
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,680
Ashura, are you all right?

314
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:54,978
Just hang in there.

315
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:57,817
His voice, the way he acted.

316
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,320
It was just like our Lord!

317
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:03,340
Only one man can mimic Lord Odin so well.

318
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,500
It's him!

319
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:06,780
Reveal yourself!

320
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:11,010
Kanjuro!

321
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:16,320
How could you say such a thing?

322
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,820
Of course I'm Odin!

323
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,880
You're hurt because of my mistake!

324
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,220
It's my fault!

325
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,320
I failed to finish him.

326
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,657
Kanjuro should be dead!

327
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:30,800
Even a sharp sword becomes
dull when pointed at a friend.

328
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:34,440
Never apologize for your kind heart.

329
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:39,640
This is nothing but a drawing.

330
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,115
Then where's Kanjuro?

331
00:20:43,420 --> 00:20:46,067
I'm manipulating the
drawing from a distance.

332
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:50,540
Unfortunately, it's rather exhausting,
especially since I'm injured.

333
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:57,757
hear that kiku from my perspective,
your blade was pretty sharp,

334
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:01,777
in fact, i'm certain that this
battle will be my final performance!

335
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:05,177
but i have an unrelenting
force that pushes

336
00:21:05,260 --> 00:21:08,797
me on my revenge towards the kozuki clan,

337
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:11,677
so i can't die just yet!

338
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,797
i shall pierce the heart of the.

339
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:17,700
Kozu-ki Clang, and I'll make
certain to do it with my own blade!

340
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,750
No!

341
00:21:25,833 --> 00:21:27,240
Lord Momonosuke is in danger!

342
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:29,177
I heard a voice earlier.

343
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:30,672
An announcement I think.

344
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:34,280
It said that Lord Momonosuke
was with Haki no Ichi.

345
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:39,200
In that case, we might
be able to reach her.

346
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:43,145
All I want to do is die in peace
and you take that away from me?

347
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:49,080
You've already lost.

348
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:52,000
You'll die here unable to stop me.

349
00:21:53,860 --> 00:21:56,880
And your dear Lord Odin will join you.

350
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:05,425
Don't you think he'd want
to go out with a pan?

351
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:12,280
Don't be angry.

352
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:18,080
We'll die together, like
good friends should.

353
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:38,580
I shall not know!

354
00:22:39,180 --> 00:22:41,060
I shall restrain him!

355
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:42,180
Knuckles!

356
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:48,220
Save our lord and stop control!

357
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:50,760
What are you doing?

358
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:52,020
Unhand me!

359
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,920
Love and grief lies, I'll go!

360
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:57,020
Asuna, don't go!

361
00:22:57,980 --> 00:23:00,980
You filthy rat! Let me go!

362
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:05,160
I curse you all, you bastard!

363
00:23:08,180 --> 00:23:13,220
I'll never defile the name
of Kozuki Odin ever again!

364
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:14,710
You're a nut!

365
00:23:57,680 --> 00:24:02,160
And now the climax, when I
shall play the lead at last.

366
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:08,700
First, I embody the Kozuki, then
I eliminate the Kozuki, and die.

367
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:13,017
An immaculate final act.

368
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:17,440
What a beautiful play my life has
been with all its twists and turns.

369
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:35,660
You bastard.

370
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:38,840
Fine then, but we're in a hurry.

371
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:41,377
You're the pain in my ass.

372
00:24:41,460 --> 00:24:44,060
They sought to protect their kings.

373
00:24:45,020 --> 00:24:48,380
Mere insects standing in my path.

374
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:51,180
God, I'll stay.

375
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:53,739
Everyone else keep pushing through.

376
00:24:55,020 --> 00:24:56,140
Good luck.

377
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:58,280
Protect Lord Momonosuke.

378
00:24:58,880 --> 00:24:59,820
Come on, King.

379
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:01,940
Let's move very well.

380
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:04,000
Please do not tarry.

381
00:25:04,340 --> 00:25:05,180
Good luck.

382
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:07,040
We're all counting on you.

383
00:25:12,800 --> 00:25:17,300
So the king of the day thinks
he can defeat me all on his own.

384
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,060
We've both been injured.

385
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,940
Quite the match-up.

386
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:23,360
Make no mistake.

387
00:25:23,780 --> 00:25:26,440
I didn't stay behind to settle a score.

388
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:29,220
I came to put an end to this.

389
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:33,120
You, Karoo, have created enough
victims, Jack. It's over!

390
00:25:34,180 --> 00:25:36,700
You have no moon to rely on.

391
00:25:36,840 --> 00:25:38,280
And you have no poison.

392
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:45,660
Seems we both will have to make do.

393
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:04,160
We gotta put this fire out quick!

394
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:06,940
The water's run out!

395
00:26:07,340 --> 00:26:08,440
Bring me more!

396
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:22,280
What the hell?

397
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:23,820
No, it can't be.

398
00:26:24,060 --> 00:26:28,100
I'm going to relish making
you traitors pay. I was sure.

399
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:29,740
Your head came off.

400
00:26:30,020 --> 00:26:31,726
You can't get back from that.

401
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:44,840
You thought you could betray me, Kaido?

402
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:50,700
Even a beheading can keep you down.

403
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:53,609
I'm sure you're not
eager for a second run.

404
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:56,715
Quite rude of Kaido, wouldn't you say?

405
00:26:57,900 --> 00:27:00,018
I'll burn this castle to the ground!

406
00:27:00,260 --> 00:27:04,820
When I'm done with it, Onigashima
will be nothing but a ball of fire!

407
00:27:05,320 --> 00:27:08,900
There's no escape up here, and no way out!

408
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:15,440
Every last one of you will die!

409
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:18,460
That's the cost of betraying me!

410
00:27:30,740 --> 00:27:34,057
Momonosuke, could you try to
change back to normal, please?

411
00:27:34,140 --> 00:27:35,434
You kind of stick out.

412
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:36,830
Oh, right.

413
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,760
Hang in there, Lord Momonosuke. Be brave.

414
00:27:47,620 --> 00:27:48,679
Sorry, I'm trying.

415
00:27:51,780 --> 00:27:55,839
Despite my shameful outburst, I have
gotten better at controlling it.

416
00:27:56,700 --> 00:27:59,171
When I first met Luffy and his associates,

417
00:27:59,340 --> 00:28:03,537
I would transform into a dragon every
time I was surprised or became sad.

418
00:28:03,620 --> 00:28:06,800
I can't help but ask, is
it like my father's power?

419
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:09,897
I wish I could turn into
a monster like he does.

420
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:12,480
At least I'd be of some use to my friends.

421
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:15,917
Luffy is still on the battlefield
fighting my father as we speak.

422
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,497
So what are we waiting for?

423
00:28:17,580 --> 00:28:20,540
I should be fighting Kaido as Odin!

424
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:22,821
Luffy's power seems to be waning.

425
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:27,140
But for some reason, he's in
very high spirits. That's good.

426
00:28:30,300 --> 00:28:32,057
Wait, I don't understand.

427
00:28:32,140 --> 00:28:33,520
How can you tell?

428
00:28:40,660 --> 00:28:44,900
How the hell are we supposed
to beat these two? Huh? Anyone?

429
00:28:45,840 --> 00:28:48,480
Everything we do bounces
right off of them.

430
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:53,700
I guess Emperors of the Sea
are just built different.

431
00:28:54,180 --> 00:28:55,637
They're trying to show off.

432
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:58,249
We can at least pretend
we've got a chance.

433
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,160
Just keep at it!

434
00:29:02,500 --> 00:29:05,265
Our attacks have to be
doing something to them!

435
00:29:05,620 --> 00:29:07,340
They're human, aren't they?

436
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:18,257
You did that earlier and it didn't work.

437
00:29:18,340 --> 00:29:19,737
Think before you attack.

438
00:29:19,820 --> 00:29:21,497
You say they're human.

439
00:29:21,580 --> 00:29:23,177
But they're nothing like us.

440
00:29:23,260 --> 00:29:24,737
That much is clear.

441
00:29:24,820 --> 00:29:25,940
So what?

442
00:29:26,060 --> 00:29:28,937
If you don't think you can beat
them Then why are you here?

443
00:29:29,020 --> 00:29:30,837
I'm just saying we need
to come up with a good

444
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:34,360
plan first We should pull
one of them away from here

445
00:29:35,100 --> 00:29:40,040
Now you're talking Those two side-by-side
are quite the gruesome spectacle

446
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:46,000
A literal vision of hell

447
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:15,740
you think this is the first
time i've been through hell

448
00:30:17,280 --> 00:30:21,398
you always have that glimmer in your
eye even when the stakes are down

449
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:28,560
you're ready to die boy you first old man

